# Script errors (`try` / `catch` / `_AdaptiveError_`)

## Prefer throw + try

AFW scripts almost never check return codes. Failures should **throw**; authors use straight-line code or `try` / `catch (e)`. Do not add soft `-1` + secondary error-string APIs (e.g. removed `get_stream_error`).

## End-to-end wiring

```text
C: AFW_THROW_ERROR_* / AFW_THROW_ERROR_RV_*
  → afw_error_t (code, message_z, rv, rv_source_id_z, rv_decoded_z, …)
  → longjmp into AFW_TRY / statement flow

catch (e) { … }
  → afw_function_execute_try (compiler_script)
  → afw_error_to_object(&this_THROWN_ERROR, …)
  → bind object to catch variable `e`
```

Object type: `generate/objects/_AdaptiveObjectType_/_AdaptiveError_.json`  
Fill: `afw_error_add_to_object()` / `afw_error_to_object()` in `error/afw_error.c`.

## Properties scripts use most

| Property | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| **`message`** | Human text from `message_z` — **primary** for users and tests |
| **`id`** | Mnemonic for the code (`general`, `not_found`, `throw`, …). **Prefer this.** Map: `AFW_ERROR_CODE_MAP` / `designs/issue-33-error-codes.md` |
| **`errorCode`** | Numeric AFW error code (may change on this beta line) |
| **`data`** | Optional payload from script `throw "msg" { … }` |
| **`rv`** | System return value when set (e.g. errno integer) |
| **`rvSourceId`** | Decoder key (`apr`, `icu`, `errno`, …) |
| **`rvDecoded`** | Decoder string (e.g. `strerror` for errno) |

Debug/flag-gated: `errorSource`, `backtrace`, `backtraceEvaluation`, parser fields, `xctxUUID`.

## C side for good catch objects

1. Put the user-visible explanation in the throw **message** (include `strerror(errno)` for OS I/O).
2. When a system code exists, use `AFW_THROW_ERROR_RV_Z` / `_FZ` with a registered **rv source** (`errno`, `apr`, `icu`) so `e.rv` / `e.rvDecoded` populate.
3. Capture `errno` **immediately** after the failing call.
4. Throw **only** through `AFW_THROW_*` macros — never hand `longjmp` to `xctx->current_try` (see **`afw-c-runtime`** and `error/afw_error.h`).

Registered errno decoder: `AFW_ERROR_RV_SOURCE_ID_Z_errno` / `"errno"` in core environment register.

## C `AFW_TRY` vs script `try`

Script `try`/`catch` is Adaptive language; C `AFW_TRY` is the runtime exception stack. Nested Adaptive eval still uses C tries underneath. `AFW_ERROR_RETHROW` in C means “run FINALLY, then rethrow to outer C try” — not script rethrow syntax.

